{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow, so the translator","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"targets SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state graph"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — computed properties, ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not imperative functions. Each row below is a rule the codegen applies; the helper","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", …) fills the gaps where a patch has no direct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"The-four-rules","level":2,"text":"The four rules"},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Pure value patch (Add, Transition\/interpolate, logic)","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"computed property \/ expression"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Interaction (Tap, Down\/press, Double Tap, Long Press)","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"gesture + ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"@GestureState","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.drag"},{"type":"text","text":" — Drag"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"drag(enable:momentum:bounds:position:translation:velocity:reset:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (helper)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"State\/memory (Switch, Sample and Hold)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" + update logic","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Animation (Classic Animation, Pop\/Spring)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":".animation(.spring)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Origami layer tree becomes the SwiftUI "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View"},{"type":"text","text":" body. Origami "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transition"},{"type":"text","text":" means"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interpolation (not SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".transition()"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier — that’s a different concept)."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Pure-value-patch-%E2%86%92-computed-property","level":3,"text":"Pure value patch → computed property"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Add","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Transition\/interpolate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and other pure-function patches carry no state.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They fan an input through math and emit an output. In SwiftUI that’s a computed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property (or an inline expression) — no ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", no side effect.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Interaction-%E2%86%92-gesture-+-State","level":3,"text":"Interaction → gesture + `@State`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s Interaction patch exposes discrete output ports: "},{"code":"down","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"position","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"onTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"onDoubleTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"onLongPress","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Each maps to a SwiftUI gesture recognizer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose output lands in "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or fires a callback. The "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction"},{"type":"text","text":" helper"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attaches only the recognizer for each output the caller requests, which keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gesture arbitration clean."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Statememory-%E2%86%92-State-+-update-logic","level":3,"text":"State\/memory → `@State` + update logic"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sample and Hold","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" remember a value across evaluations. That’s what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is for. Codegen emits the state variable plus the update path (a gesture","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"callback, a ","type":"text"},{"code":".onChange","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or an assignment inside a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" block)."}]},{"text":"Animation → `withAnimation` \/ `.animation`","type":"heading","anchor":"Animation-%E2%86%92-withAnimation--animation","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Classic Animation"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pop Animation"},{"type":"text","text":", and other animation patches drive a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"toward a target over time. In SwiftUI, that’s a state change wrapped in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" or an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(_:value:)"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier on the animated property."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Continuous-time springs that don’t have a stock SwiftUI equivalent get flagged"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by the parser — Swami won’t fake them."}]},{"text":"Flag, don’t fake","type":"heading","anchor":"Flag-dont-fake","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Some Origami semantics don’t have a SwiftUI equivalent. When the parser hits one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it emits a marker in the IR and codegen surfaces the gap rather than papering over","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it. The current list: continuous-time springs, custom JavaScript patches,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"absolute-position layout.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swami\/origamimappings"]}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How Swami translates the four kinds of Origami patch into SwiftUI’s state graph."}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Swami"}],"title":"Origami → SwiftUI mappings","role":"article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Reference","anchor":"Reference","identifie